    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain how lisinopril actually works in the raas pathway? i need to understand the specific steps for my exam",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril, an ACE inhibitor, works by blocking the Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme (ACE). This enzyme is crucial in the Renin-Angiotensin-Aldosterone System (RAAS) pathway, as it converts Angiotensin I into the potent vasoconstrictor, Angiotensin II. By inhibiting ACE, lisinopril prevents the formation of Angiotensin II, which in turn reduces blood pressure and decreases aldosterone secretion. This overall effect leads to vasodilation and reduced fluid retention.",
      "source": "target",
